+// Soft TLB (PS4 port). An entry maps one 4 KiB guest page to its host RAM page. It is filled only
+// by a successful translated guest read (read table) or write (write table) of plain RAM, so the
+// R and C bits in the page table are already set exactly as the full path would set them. The tag
+// holds the translation mode (MSR.DR) and the entry the segment register it was translated with,
+// so mode and segment changes need no flush; tlbie, BAT, SDR1, segment-register and page table
+// updates, resets and state loads flush everything. Memory checks, the data cache emulation and
+// write-through/cache-inhibited pages always take the full path.
+static inline u32 SoftTlbTag(const PowerPC::PowerPCState& ppc_state, u32 address)
+{
+  return (address >> HW_PAGE_INDEX_SHIFT) | (ppc_state.msr.DR ? 0x100000u : 0u) | 0x200000u;
